WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.000
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.100
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.670
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:26.450
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:34.190
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.660
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.530
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:44.270
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.930
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.610
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:01.680
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.650
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:12.300
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.200
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.440
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:32.550
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:37.290
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:42.020
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.150
Return to the darkness

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.490
with your odious fate...

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.200
Ayumu Narumi...

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.500
Tell me...

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.730
Why are we alive?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.940
<i>I'm not my brother...</i>

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:23.380
<i>Nor am I a Blade Child...</i>

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.220
<i>What can I possibly answer?</i>

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.790
<i>"Relentless Rain"
What can I possibly answer?</i>

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.260
"Relentless Rain"

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.720
<i>You'll never be Kiyotaka-san!</i>

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.950
What are they thinking,
going that fast?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.820
What's wrong with that?

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.750
It's up to them how
they use their lives.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:51.630
They're simply living
by their own rules.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.420
And you'd like to say the
same for the Blade Children?

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.730
You're a Blade Child too, aren't you?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.210
It certainly is hard to see...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:08.200
I hope the rain lets up
in the morning...

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.220
I can't believe I can sleep
at a time like this.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.410
"Hiyono Yuizaki"

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.710
Good morning.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.880
<i>Rutherford-sama,
I've brought your breakfast.</i>

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.220
<i>Rutherford-sama...</i>

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>Rutherford-sama?</i>

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.220
Come back...

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.770
I bought us some breakfast.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.220
Let's start picking up the phone, okay?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.620
Do you need something?

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.110
Let's go have breakfast!

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.630
The weather is so nice today!

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:09.430
It's like yesterday's rain
even cleared the air!

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:13.530
Not going outside on a day
like this would be a huge waste!

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.260
Let's go!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.970
Return to the darkness

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.200
with your odious fate...

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:01.170
<i>Come on, Ryoko!</i>

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.520
Here you are!

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.790
The weather is nice out,
but I warmed it up anyway!

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.290
Here.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.530
Don't look so fixedly.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.560
Even I can make rice balls!

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.710
Mmm! Isn't it delicious?!

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:32.780
I've never tasted anything
quite like it before!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.220
Go ahead, eat right up!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.240
Sure...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.930
Make yourself at home...

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:57.260
The bread they make there
is really delicious!

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.710
What is it you want?

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.340
Why did you approach me?

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.780
Why did you sit me
in the passenger seat?

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.790
<i>You know Kiyotaka-san, don't you?</i>

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.690
Tell me about him.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.530
What for?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.150
How is he?

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:25.100
I bet you'd like to see him,
wouldn't you?

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.030
But think about it.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.800
If he is alive...

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.200
...why won't he contact you at all?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.780
In the end, even if he is alive,

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.380
he wouldn't want anyone's help.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.720
Not even from you.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.150
What's your point?

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.420
That's the type of
person Kiyotaka is...

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.330
And besides,

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:58.320
I don't consider him
all that almighty.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.910
"Ryoko Takamachi"

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:27.120
<i>Why couldn't we save him?</i>

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:39.160
I guess there's no opposing destiny.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.470
Not for the Blade Children...

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.650
Who exactly are you people?

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.490
That's tough to answer.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.400
It seems like your existence
would be inconvenienced

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.730
if the world learned about you...

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:08.430
I suppose it's something
along those lines...

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:12.570
Or maybe that we mustn't exist...

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.840
But there's no way
for us to determine

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:20.080
if we're inconvenienced or
that we shouldn't exist.

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:24.780
As long as we exist, all we
can do is continue living.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.810
Or should we disappear
from this world?

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.320
Doesn't sound like I'll get
a straight answer out of you.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:37.130
It's only natural to be afraid.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.800
Afraid? Of what?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.330
Why did you come with me?

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.640
You can't keep believing.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.810
You wonder if Kiyotaka
really has abandoned you...

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.710
You're uneasy about
learning the truth...

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.410
<i>I have faith in Kiyotaka-san!</i>

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:01.220
No. No, you don't.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.760
You're uneasy.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.730
I just want to help him!

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.090
And you want to be needed.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.270
Kiyotaka disappeared
before your very eyes.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.710
He vanished without so much as a word.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.340
There's no need to act tough.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.310
I am not acting tough!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:24.330
You're not wrong.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.310
You're not wrong at all.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.310
You should be honest with yourself.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:36.390
You'll only grow exhausted
by believing and waiting.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.880
That was great!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.370
Now that our stomachs are full,
what should we do?

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.550
Is there anywhere you'd like to go?

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.020
I leave it up to you.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.720
In that case...

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.290
I guess something outdoorsy
would be nice!

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:18.730
It's warm out, and I feel
like relaxing in the sun.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.230
Yeah...

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.140
For now, let's take a walk
to settle our meal.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:28.270
Actually, how would you
like some pasta?

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:29.040
Alright.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:33.310
Great! I found this adorable new place

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.350
and I've always wanted to give it a try!

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:41.450
But it's just not the same going alone...

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.580
Thank you for coming with...

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.620
Wait!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.670
Ryoko?

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:55.370
Don't worry about me.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:56.570
Where are you?

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:58.370
You don't need to worry about me.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.860
You at home?

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.280
Ryoko?

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.480
Ryoko?

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.910
I knew...

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.080
I knew from the very start...

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.120
Don't talk like that! I'll figure out...

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.120
We're up against fate,
there's nothing we can do...

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.890
But I'll at least make sure you're...

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:22.460
It's pointless. After all,
I'm a Blade Child too...

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.450
Which is why I'll try to...

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.910
What am I waiting for?

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.150
How will waiting exhaust me?

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:45.720
Whenever I watch the flow of water,
my mind grows calm...

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.480
Do you know why?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.060
Because we were born from the ocean.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:57.720
All life began there. All of it...

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:01.800
Yet, we're unable to return to it.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.540
If we're to live in a
world of nothing but suffering,

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.610
then perhaps we should cease to exist...

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:11.010
Why should we do that?

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.280
Death is natural Providence;

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:15.680
it's not something to be feared.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.210
It's just that...

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:29.290
It's just that it's
painful being alone...

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:35.840
Talk to me. It might help.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.900
I'd like to know for myself.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.910
I'd like to see the ends of destiny.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.710
Then it's not too late!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.710
No, it is.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:47.080
Thanks to Kiyotaka
and that brother of his.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:01.590
You're not going to say anything,
are you?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.470
<i>Narumi-san! What happened last night?!</i>

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.870
-Nothing...
-Liar!

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:12.070
Something happened-
what was it?!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.810
Nothing. It's just that...

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:16.440
It's just what?

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:20.750
It's just that it all ended.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.710
It all ended?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.040
Hi.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:35.550
<i>Eyes-kun hasn't come back yet.</i>

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.200
He went somewhere...

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.960
Help me...

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:48.670
<i>Kiyotaka thinks highly of
Ayumu-kun for some reason.</i>

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:52.010
He says he's the key to the
Blade Children's salvation.

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:55.310
<i>Ayumu-kun has gotten too involved.</i>

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:59.750
You're not after me-
you're after Ayumu...

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:09.280
Hello? Please, say something...

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.200
<i>I can't...</i>

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.810
Why did you do that?!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.540
Don't worry about me anymore.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.440
You'll just be wasting your time.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:28.310
Why did you do that?! She was crying!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.380
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.720
Leave me alone...

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.790
Why...Why?

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.420
<i>This isn't like you, Narumi-san!</i>

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.790
I'll always be like this.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:41.450
Not a single thing has ever
brought me satisfaction.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.730
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:46.900
I'm done.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:02.210
<i>The Narumi-san I know seems
to have run off somewhere.</i>

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.650
I guess I'll just wait
until he comes back!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.490
<i>If you ever bump into
Narumi-san somewhere,</i>

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.530
tell him to be energetic!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.790
Bye now!

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:25.340
Giving a suffering person
false hope is a sin.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:28.340
It's unforgivable.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.140
The reason being...

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.880
...that fate is unalterable.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.140
Everything is determined
from the beginning.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:40.950
Just as everyone has "death"...

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.160
Perhaps it was even
pre-determined that Kiyotaka

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.150
would abandon you...

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.460
Have a nice trip.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:00.170
What are you planning to do to Ayumu?!

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.710
Open this up!

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.440
I know you can hear me!
Open the door!

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.610
<i>Let us begin, Ayumu Narumi...</i>

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:32.340
<i>I'll always be like this.</i>

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:37.470
<i>Not a single thing has ever
brought me satisfaction.</i>

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:43.950
<i>Don't worry about me anymore!</i>

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.250
<i>Stop it...</i>

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.620
<i>Stop it!</i>

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:54.020
<i>Stop!</i>

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:59.190
<i>Don't worry about me!</i>

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:03.900
Oh! It's you!

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.410
<i>Nice to meet you, Ayumu-kun!</i>

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:09.770
<i>Madoka!</i>

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:19.780
<i>Madoka!</i>

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:32.430
Yeah?

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.560
I have your Madoka.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.770
What have you done with her?

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.550
Wait!

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.610
I have no intention to get
involved with you any further!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.150
Come with me...

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:11.660
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:18.360
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:36.520
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:42.160
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:48.060
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:54.640
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.640 --> 00:22:00.380
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:05.580
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:11.420
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:23.030
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:28.800
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:35.110
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:41.210
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:45.040
Will a demon or a serpent come out?

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:48.210
It's do or die! The die is cast!

00:22:48.210 --> 00:22:50.480
The finger's on the trigger
and time's almost up!

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:53.220
Will the mute Mermaid Princess
be the one to disappear,

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.950
or the seagull-riding boy?!

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:58.220
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:00.020
The Man in the High Castle

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:03.160
If you see a rainbow in
the sky after a rain shower,

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:05.060
then you mustn't get lost anymore!

00:23:05.060 --> 00:23:07.430
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
